        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computer Vision",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Classical image processing and DSP practitioners already know convolutional filters —\nthey just hand-designed them. CNNs learn the same filters from data:"
    },
    {
      "id": "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md#006",
      "path": [
        "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:data-science:15-computer-vision, git-history:data-science:15-computer-vision]",
        "canonical_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "current_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "id": "maxim:data-science:computer-vision",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "data-science",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "section": "data-science",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computer Vision",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nClassical image processing filter          CNN equivalent\n──────────────────────────────────────     ────────────────────────────────────────────\nGaussian blur (low-pass filter):           Smooth activation map in early layers\n  K = [[1,2,1],[2,4,2],[1,2,1]]/16          First layer filters often resemble Gabor\n  → attenuates high frequencies               filters (oriented Gaussians) = learned\n  → removes noise                             blur + edge in one kernel"
    },
    {
      "id": "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md#007",
      "path": [
        "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:data-science:15-computer-vision, git-history:data-science:15-computer-vision]",
        "canonical_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "current_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "id": "maxim:data-science:computer-vision",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "data-science",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "section": "data-science",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computer Vision",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sobel operator (edge detection):           Learned 3×3 edge detector in layer 1\n  K_x = [[-1,0,1],[-2,0,2],[-1,0,1]]       AlexNet, VGG layer 1 filters ≈ Sobel-like\n  → ∂I/∂x ← gradient in x direction         on Gabor basis\n  K_y = Kᵀ                                  Network discovers these automatically"
    },
    {
      "id": "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md#008",
      "path": [
        "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:data-science:15-computer-vision, git-history:data-science:15-computer-vision]",
        "canonical_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "current_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "id": "maxim:data-science:computer-vision",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "data-science",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "section": "data-science",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computer Vision",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Laplacian of Gaussian (LoG):               Deep layer features: corners, textures\n  ∇²(G*I) ← second derivative              LoG is a \"corner detector\" — layer 2/3\n  Used in: blob detection, SIFT              CNNs learn these"
    },
    {
      "id": "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md#009",
      "path": [
        "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:data-science:15-computer-vision, git-history:data-science:15-computer-vision]",
        "canonical_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "current_path": "data-science/15-COMPUTER-VISION.md",
        "id": "maxim:data-science:computer-vision",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "data-science",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[computer, vision]",
        "section": "data-science",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computer Vision",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sharpening filter:                         High-pass component in residual learning\n  K = [[0,-1,0],[-1,5,-1],[0,-1,0]]        ResNet's F(x) = H(x) - x is the residual\n  = I + Laplacian                           \"high-frequency\" part on top of identity"
    },
    {
      "id": "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md#010",
      "path": [
        "15-COMPUTER-VISION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:data-science:15-computer-vision, git-history:data-science:15-computer-vision]",
